{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":71243,"duration_api_ms":108067,"num_turns":5,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8d5c9205-9285-40e7-a5b0-070cd25adebd","total_cost_usd":0.37071635,"usage":{"input_tokens":860,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25366,"cache_read_input_tokens":78226,"output_tokens":1809,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25366,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":135,"outputTokens":5925,"cacheReadInputTokens":324821,"cacheCreationInputTokens":49039,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.12354085000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":860,"outputTokens":1809,"cacheReadInputTokens":78226,"cacheCreationInputTokens":25366,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2471755,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All three amendments identify genuine, verified defects in the codebase. fr-7-f0d55cc5 correctly flags partial state mutation before validation completion in enforce_invariants, with fragile test assertions that only hold due to current default state values. fr-7-6c8fdcb3 identifies a real mass-accounting inconsistency where reserve_g accumulates from feeding but is never debited for hatching/maturation, which instead pull from dissolved water pools. fr-7-baf66be2 correctly identifies that the budget guard is disabled wholesale by any action flux rather than applying the residual-subtraction pattern already used for chemistry carbon.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-7-f0d55cc5","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in invariants.rs: enforce_invariants clamps DO (line 7), pH (line 95), and 40+ indices (lines 109-127) on &mut TankState before reaching later validation checks like check_unit_interval for shrimp_assimilation_efficiency (line 185+) and check_non_negative for reserve_g (line 129). If a later check returns Err, the state is already partially mutated. The validation.rs tests (lines 92-127) assert engine.full_state() == &expected after error, which only passes because TankState::new() with the test seed produces values where all clamp operations are no-ops. Any change to defaults or seeds could break these assertions. Both proposed fixes (reorder validation before clamping, or remove fragile assertions) are sound."},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-6c8fdcb3","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in shrimp.rs: reserve_g is documented in biology.rs (lines 85-91) as 'the retained share of feeding that has not yet been used for growth/reproduction' and is populated by route_consumed_food (lines 230-235). However, both hatching (line 443, via fund_hatched_clutch_from_water) and maturation (line 530, via fund_live_shrimp_biomass_from_water) pull exclusively from dissolved water pools (DON, TAN, DOC, DIC) at lines 626-656, never touching reserve_g. reserve_g is only decremented during mortality (lines 602-607, transfer to detritus). This makes reserve_g an ever-accumulating dead-end pool that contradicts the documented routing contract. The fix—debiting reserve_g first, then water pools as fallback—correctly aligns implementation with documentation."},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-baf66be2","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in engine.rs: tick_has_closed_system_nitrogen/carbon (lines 563-575) return false whenever ANY entry matches the 5 action labels with non-zero flux, completely disabling the budget guard for the entire tick. A tick with a legitimate water_change AND an unrelated nitrogen leak will never trigger BudgetImbalance. The code already implements the correct residual-subtraction pattern for chemistry carbon (lines 577-589, carbon_guard_delta_mg subtracts chemistry_external_carbon_flux_mg). Applying the same pattern to action fluxes—subtracting known action deltas from the residual rather than disabling the guard entirely—would correctly detect unexplained drift in mixed ticks while accounting for known open-system exchanges."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"2a90d379-d423-4abf-8020-9a579f96d650"}
